            {# ── Slide 2: What Parachute is (three-layer model) ── #}
            <section class="pi-slide fade-up fade-up-3" data-slide-id="2" data-video-start="15" data-video-end="55">
                <p class="pi-label">What Parachute is</p>
                <h2 class="pi-h2">A personal memory and knowledge layer<br>for <em>your</em> data and <em>your</em> AI.</h2>
                <div class="pi-flywheel">
                    <div class="pi-flywheel-row">
                        <div class="pi-flywheel-role">Vault</div>
                        <div class="pi-flywheel-body"><strong>The memory + knowledge layer.</strong> Notes, tags, links.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pi-flywheel-row">
                        <div class="pi-flywheel-role">Intelligence</div>
                        <div class="pi-flywheel-body"><strong>Bring the AI you trust</strong> to any vault &mdash; over MCP + the open API.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="pi-flywheel-row">
                        <div class="pi-flywheel-role">Surface</div>
                        <div class="pi-flywheel-body"><strong>Custom web interfaces</strong> over your data.</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <aside class="pi-notes">
                    <p>Parachute helps you organize your thoughts, notes, and projects in a coherent way &mdash; without architecting the perfect system first. Add things in, be in easy conversation with your AI.</p>
                    <p>Think of it as bringing together the best of what Obsidian offers (notes, tags, links, files on your machine) and what Notion offers (a clean place to organize a project, a life, a team) &mdash; in a truly personal interface.</p>
                    <p><strong>Vault</strong> is self-hostable and customizable. <strong>Intelligence</strong> means you bring the AI you trust to the data you own. <strong>Surfaces</strong> let you navigate, view, share, and interact with your data however fits.</p>
                    <p>Every vault is reachable over an <strong>open REST API</strong> &mdash; so people can build whatever interface they want on top &mdash; and over <strong>MCP</strong>, so any AI system you use instantly works with your data.</p>
                    <p>The three layers are the conceptual model. Underneath them sit the modules that ship today (vault, scribe, surface, hub, runner) &mdash; we'll get to those in a moment.</p>
                </aside>
            </section>

            {# ── Slide 3: Voice-first origin ── #}
