                <aside class="pi-notes">
                    <p><strong>Vault</strong> is your data: notes, tags, links, files. Runs on your machine or our cloud. Reachable over an open REST API and MCP &mdash; so any tool can read and write to it.</p>
                    <p><strong>Intelligence</strong> is the AI you trust (Claude, GPT, local), brought to the data you own &mdash; over MCP and the open REST API. For scheduled or automated agent work, <strong>Runner</strong> runs a prompt on a schedule against your vault.</p>
                    <p><strong>Surface</strong> is your interface: custom web views to navigate, share, and interact with your data. Notes (the PWA) is one surface we ship; build your own, or use what we make.</p>
                    <p>The three layers sit on top of a few small modules that ship today &mdash; <strong>vault</strong>, <strong>scribe</strong> (transcription), <strong>surface</strong> (the UI host that bundles Notes), <strong>hub</strong> (the coordinator that handles auth), <strong>runner</strong> (a prompt on a schedule against your vault).</p>
                    <p>The contract underneath: every vault speaks an <strong>open REST API</strong> and <strong>MCP</strong> &mdash; the open standard every major lab now supports. That's what makes the substrate portable: you don't depend on us to use your data.</p>
